eeds a trustline on the destination account — see `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`#build`,children:`requirements and limitations`}),`.`]})]}),_jsxs(`section`,{className:`deploy`,id:`deploy`,\"aria-labelledby\":`usdt0-dep-h`,children:[_jsxs(`div`,{className:`dep-head`,children:[_jsx(`h2`,{id:`usdt0-dep-h`,children:`Deploy — adding USDT0 to your environment`}),_jsx(`span`,{className:`live`,children:`Live on Stellar Mainnet`})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`dep-body`,children:[_jsxs(`p`,{className:`dep-lead`,children:[`USDT0 is live on Stellar Mainnet. Add it to your wallet or environment. Test your integration by `,_jsx(`strong`,{children:`moving a small amount end to end`}),` before rolling out to your users.`]}),_jsx(`a`,{className:`dep-link`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,href:`https://stellar.expert/explorer/public/asset/USDT0-GATISXX6BZ6NC7IKQBY37CJD4SOZL3CYZJWXEDG6JVIY4WBS6KXJHN6Q`,children:`View the asset on stellar.expert →`}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`ids`,children:IDS.map(([label,note,value],i)=>_jsxs(`div`,{className:`id-row`,children:[_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`id-label`,children:label}),_jsx(`p`,{className:`id-note`,children:note})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`id-val`,children:[_jsx(`code`,{id:`usdt0-id-${i}`,children:value}),_jsx(`button`,{className:`copy`,type:`button`,\"aria-label\":`Copy ${label}`,onClick:()=>copy(i),children:copyLabels[i]||`Copy`})]})]},label))}),_jsx(`a`,{className:`dep-link`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,href:`https://docs.usdt0.to/technical-documentation/deployments?q=stellar`,children:`Contract deployments on docs.usdt0.to →`})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`dep-note`,children:[_jsxs(`b`,{children:[_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://stellar.expert/explorer/public/asset/USDT0-GATISXX6BZ6NC7IKQBY37CJD4SOZL3CYZJWXEDG6JVIY4WBS6KXJHN6Q`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`This asset`}),` sets `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`auth_revocable`}),` and `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`auth_clawback_enabled`})]}),` — the issuer can revoke a trustline or `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/build/guides/transactions/clawbacks`,children:`clawback a balance`}),`. `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`auth_required`}),` is not set, so anyone can hold it. 💡 Soroswap maintains an `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://github.com/soroswap/token-list/tree/main/assets`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`ecosystem token list`}),` covering both classic assets and contract tokens (community-maintained rather than an official Stellar registry, and widely used).`]})]}),_jsxs(`section`,{className:`notes-sec`,id:`build`,\"aria-labelledby\":`usdt0-bd-h`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`dep-head`,children:_jsx(`h2`,{id:`usdt0-bd-h`,children:`Before you build — requirements and limitations`})}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`notes-body`,children:[_jsx(`p`,{className:`dep-lead`,children:`What USDT0 on Stellar requires for integration.`}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`notes`,children:[_jsxs(`div`,{className:`note`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`ntag`,children:`Trustlines`}),_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`A trustline has to exist before the first payment lands.`}),` Sending USDT0 to an account that has no USDT0 trustline fails with `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/data/apis/horizon/api-reference/errors/result-codes/operation-specific/payment`,children:_jsx(`code`,{children:`op_no_trust`})}),`. A wallet may create it for you when you swap into USDT0 in-app; a transfer arriving from an exchange or another wallet has no such fallback. If you custody for users, create it during onboarding — `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/build/guides/transactions/sponsored-reserves`,children:`sponsored reserves`}),` can cover the reserve.`]})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`note`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`ntag`,children:`Decimals`}),_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`The OFT reconciles a precision gap for you.`}),` USDT0 on Stellar carries `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/learn/fundamentals/stellar-data-structures/assets`,children:`seven decimals`}),`; cross-chain transfers normalize to the OFT’s `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://docs.layerzero.network/v2/concepts/technical-reference/oft-reference`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`six shared decimals`}),`. Send 1.2345678 and 1.234567 moves; the remaining 0.0000008 is floored off as dust and refunded to you before the debit. Nothing to convert by hand — but account for it when you calculate or display an amount.`]})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`note`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`ntag`,children:`Route limits`}),_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`A route can enforce a minimum.`}),` Minimum transfer amounts are set per contract, so call `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://docs.usdt0.to/technical-documentation/developer`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:_jsx(`code`,{children:`quote_oft`})}),` for the route you intend to use rather than assuming any amount will go through.`]})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`note`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`ntag`,children:`Backing`}),_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`The backing sits in one contract.`}),` USDT0's adapter on Ethereum holds the USDT behind the natively issued supply.`]})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`note`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`ntag`,children:`Yield`}),_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`USDT0 doesn't accrue yield.`}),` It earns nothing sitting in a balance — any return has to come from the market you supply it to.`]})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{className:`note`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`ntag`,children:`Listings`}),_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[_jsx(`b`,{children:`Each venue decides which networks it supports.`}),` One USDT0 doesn't mean every listing offers every route, so check what a partner actually enables before you send users to it.`]})]})]})]})]}),_jsxs(`section`,{className:`notes-sec`,id:`faq`,\"aria-labelledby\":`usdt0-fq-h`,children:[_jsx(`div`,{className:`dep-head`,children:_jsx(`h2`,{id:`usdt0-fq-h`,children:`FAQ`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`notes-body`,children:_jsxs(`div`,{className:`faqs`,children:[_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`Is USDT0 the same as USDT?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsx(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:`No — it is a separate asset with its own contract, worth the same and backed 1:1 by USDT locked on Ethereum. The practical difference is deposits: a venue that supports USDT will not necessarily accept USDT0 on Stellar. Check your destination lists USDT0 on Stellar specifically before you send.`})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`Which USDT0 on Stellar is the real one?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`The one issued by `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`GATISXX6BZ6NC7IKQBY37CJD4SOZL3CYZJWXEDG6JVIY4WBS6KXJHN6Q`}),` —`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://stellar.expert/explorer/public/asset/USDT0-GATISXX6BZ6NC7IKQBY37CJD4SOZL3CYZJWXEDG6JVIY4WBS6KXJHN6Q`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`check it on Stellar Expert`}),`. Asset codes on Stellar are not unique — anyone can issue an asset called USDT0 — so identity is the code `,_jsx(`b`,{children:`and`}),` the issuer together. Pin that issuer, and confirm the contract you derive from it matches `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`CBSJZEIO5C7KC2SF3MKSNXXJSW5G3VTNBX4ATMKUI3B2MR4JKM4R26YF`}),`.`]})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsxs(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:[`Why did my USDT0 payment fail with `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`op_no_trust`}),`?`]})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`The destination account has no USDT0 trustline, and one must exist before the first payment can land. A wallet often creates it when a user swaps into USDT0 in-app, but a transfer arriving from an exchange or another wallet has no such fallback. If you custody for users, create it during onboarding —`,` `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/build/guides/transactions/sponsored-reserves`,children:`sponsored reserves`}),` `,`can cover the reserve.`]})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`How long does a transfer to Stellar take?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`It depends on the chain you send from, not on Stellar. Stellar finalises in about 5 seconds; the wait is the source chain confirming and LayerZero verifying the message. From Polygon it is about a minute. From Ethereum, Arbitrum, Tron and Solana — the routes carrying most volume — expect roughly 18–21 minutes. A few low-traffic routes take hours. The`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://usdt0.to/transfer`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`transfer UI`}),` `,`quotes an estimate for your route before you send.`]})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`Why is my transfer slower than I expected?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`Usually because the figure you saw was a network-wide best case rather than your route. Nothing on the Stellar side is the bottleneck. If a transfer runs well past the estimate you were quoted, look up the message on`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://layerzeroscan.com/analytics/networks`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`LayerZero Scan`}),`, which indexes Stellar as a destination, to see which step it is sitting at. USDT0 lists`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://docs.usdt0.to/resources/contact`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`support contacts`}),` `,`for transfers that stall.`]})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`What does it cost to bring USDT0 to Stellar?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`Three separate things, and two different calls report them. USDT0's own protocol fee is zero on most routes and 0.03% where one applies:`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://docs.usdt0.to/technical-documentation/developer/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:_jsx(`code`,{children:`quote_oft`})}),` `,`shows it as the gap between `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`amount_sent_ld`}),` and `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`amount_received_ld`}),`, so read it there rather than trusting a published number. The LayerZero messaging fee is separate and comes back from`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://docs.usdt0.to/technical-documentation/developer/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:_jsx(`code`,{children:`quote_send`})}),`, paid in XLM when you send from Stellar — this is the part that varies most. And on Stellar, ordinary transactions cost a`,` `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/learn/fundamentals/fees-resource-limits-metering`,children:`minimum of 100 stroops`}),` `,`per operation, which is unrelated to bridging.`]})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`What is the difference between the Open Mesh and the Legacy Mesh?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`On the Open Mesh each chain runs its own OFT contract, and moving between them burns on one side and mints on the other. The`,` `,_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://docs.usdt0.to/overview/the-legacy-mesh`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`Legacy Mesh`}),` `,`connects chains where Tether had already deployed native USDT — Ethereum, Tron, TON, Arbitrum, Solana and Celo — through a shared non-custodial hub on Arbitrum, so those chains keep their existing USDT contracts rather than migrating.`]})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`Why did I receive slightly less than I sent?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsx(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:`Rounding, in the last decimal places only. USDT0 on Stellar carries seven decimals; cross-chain transfers normalise to the OFT's six shared decimals. Send 1.2345678 and 1.234567 moves — the remaining 0.0000008 is floored off as dust and refunded to you before the debit.`})})]}),_jsxs(`details`,{className:`faq`,children:[_jsx(`summary`,{children:_jsx(`span`,{className:`fq`,children:`Who can freeze or clawback USDT0 on Stellar?`})}),_jsx(`div`,{className:`fa`,children:_jsxs(`p`,{className:`ncopy`,children:[`The issuer. The asset sets `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`auth_revocable`}),` and `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`auth_clawback_enabled`}),`, so the issuer can revoke a trustline or`,` `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/build/guides/transactions/clawbacks`,children:`clawback a balance`}),`.`,` `,_jsx(`code`,{children:`auth_required`}),` is not set, so anyone can hold it without approval.`]})})]})]})})]}),_jsxs(`dl`,{className:`spec`,children:[_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`dt`,{children:`Asset`}),_jsx(`dd`,{children:`USDT0`})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`dt`,{children:`Transfer`}),_jsx(`dd`,{children:_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://usdt0.to/transfer`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`usdt0.to`})})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`dt`,{children:`Networks`}),_jsx(`dd`,{children:_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://analytics.usdt0.to/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`26+`})})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`dt`,{children:`USDT in circulation`}),_jsx(`dd`,{children:_jsx(`a`,{href:`https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/tether/`,target:`_blank`,rel:`noopener noreferrer`,children:`$180B+`})})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`dt`,{children:`Stellar settlement`}),_jsx(`dd`,{children:_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/docs/learn/fundamentals/stellar-stack`,children:`~5s`})})]}),_jsxs(`div`,{children:[_jsx(`dt`,{children:`Stellar fee`}),_jsx(`dd`,{children: